# ConstellAI

Physics-informed autonomous orbital intelligence for space traffic management — Temporal Graph Neural Networks + Multi-Agent Reinforcement Learning for constellation-scale conjunction forecasting and collision-avoidance coordination.

Target venues: AIAA SciTech, IEEE Aerospace Conference, NeurIPS/ICLR workshops
Timeline: 8–10 months · Team: 4 developers + 1 industry mentor

## Overview

ConstellAI models Earth's orbital environment as a dynamic graph, forecasts conjunctions multiple days ahead, and coordinates constellation-wide avoidance maneuvers under fuel constraints — using public TLE data, orbital mechanics, temporal graph learning, and multi-agent RL.

Every module carries an explicit physics or learning-theoretic justification, recorded in `docs/adr/`.

## Architecture

| Module | Path | Responsibility | Owner(s) |
|---|---|---|---|
| Orbital Mechanics Core (M1) | `constellai/orbital_mechanics/` | TLE ingestion, SGP4 propagation, frame transforms, perturbations, conjunction geometry | Dev A + Dev B |
| Graph Construction (M2) | `constellai/graph/` | Dynamic graph construction, temporal windowing, feature engineering | Dev C |
| TGNN Forecasting (M3) | `constellai/models/tgnn/` | Temporal GNN — conjunction probability / time-to-closest-approach | Dev C |
| MARL Coordination (M4) | `constellai/models/marl/` | Multi-agent RL — coordinated avoidance maneuver policies | Dev D |
| Simulation & Evaluation (M5) | `constellai/simulation/` | Independent ground-truth simulator, scenario generation, metrics | Dev A + Dev B |
| Infra / MLOps (M6) | — | Experiment tracking, CI/CD, benchmarking | Dev D |

Interface contracts between modules (units, frames, tensor shapes) are frozen in `docs/adr/` before implementation begins.

## Repository Structure

```
constellai/
├── constellai/
│   ├── orbital_mechanics/      # M1
│   ├── graph/                  # M2
│   ├── models/
│   │   ├── tgnn/                # M3
│   │   └── marl/                # M4
│   ├── simulation/             # M5
│   └── common/                  # shared constants, types, config schemas
├── experiments/configs/         # one YAML per experiment run
├── tests/
│   ├── unit/
│   ├── integration/
│   └── physics_validation/
├── docs/
│   ├── adr/                     # Architecture Decision Records
│   └── research_log/
└── paper/                        # LaTeX source, figures, tables
```

## Getting Started

```bash
git clone https://github.com/<org>/constellai.git
cd constellai
poetry install
pre-commit install
pytest tests/unit
```

## Roadmap

- [ ] Step 0 — Environment & repo setup (CI, pre-commit, experiment tracking)
- [ ] Step 1 — Literature review and gap analysis
- [ ] Step 2 — M1 + M5: propagator validated against Vallado test vectors, ground-truth simulator
- [ ] Step 3 — Non-ML baseline (TCA/miss-distance threshold)
- [ ] Step 4 — M2 + M3: graph pipeline, TGNN prototype vs. baseline
- [ ] Step 5 — M4: MARL environment, single-agent then multi-agent training
- [ ] Step 6 — Integration: TGNN forecasts feed MARL state/reward
- [ ] Step 7 — Scalability and sensitivity analysis
- [ ] Step 8 — Paper and capstone prep

## Development Workflow

- Branching: `main` (protected, tagged per milestone) ← `develop` ← `feature/<module>-<desc>`
- PRs target `develop`, minimum 1 reviewer; new models or physics assumptions require a `needs-science-review` tag
- No hardcoded hyperparameters — experiment configs live in `experiments/configs/`

## Team

Dev A, Dev B — M1, M5 · Dev C — M2, M3 · Dev D — M4, M6 · Industry Mentor — cross-module review

Integration lead rotates monthly.

